<title>FRANCE: AGF completes sale of SAFR stake.</title>
<headline>AGF completes sale of SAFR stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer AGF said on Friday it had completed the planned sale of its 47 percent stake in Societe Anonyme Francaise de Reassurances (SAFR) for 2.529 billion French francs to Swiss Re.</p>
<p>AGF said in a statement the sale took place pursuant to a definitive agreement signed and announced on February 26.</p>
<p>AGF said the sale &quot;completes the process of refocusing on (its) core business&quot;.</p>
<p>It said it was also acquiring a 14 percent stake in the Euler Group for 765 million francs, with the payment and delivery of shares occurring prior to June 30.</p>
<p>Euler is majority owned by AGF.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
